<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; To the Public Records Officer, Department =
of Administrative Services:<br><br>This is a request under ORS 192.311 to 1=
92.478. I am also giving notice of my intent to petition the Attorney Gener=
al regarding two prior requests, addressed at the end of this message.<br><=
br>I am Robert Samuel White, date of birth April 11, 1977. I served as a vo=
lunteer with the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department at Jessie M. Honeym=
an Memorial State Park in February and March 2025. I was dismissed on March=
 24, 2025, and permanently excluded from all OPRD volunteer programs on Mar=
ch 26, 2025, in a letter citing my public comments about staff. On March 24=
, 2026, Oregon State Police and a United States Forest Service special agen=
t were sent to my residence on restricted federal land.<br><br>I request th=
e following records for the period February 1, 2025 to the present, except =
as otherwise specified.<br><br>1. All records concerning me held by DAS in =
any division, including the Chief Human Resources Office, Risk Management, =
Enterprise Goods and Services, and the Office of the Director. This include=
s records indexed under Robert White, Robert Samuel White, Robert S. White,=
 Sam White, or my date of birth.<br><br>2. All records reflecting any behav=
ioral threat assessment, threat management, workplace violence assessment, =
or safety planning process concerning me. This includes but is not limited =
to: workplace violence incident reports; reports made under Statewide HR Po=
licy 50.010.02; threat assessment team or workplace violence prevention tea=
m records, agendas, minutes, notes, or referrals; completed or partial asse=
ssment instruments of any kind; designations of me as a subject of concern,=
 person of concern, or equivalent; safety plans; no-contact or no-trespass =
directives; and any recommendation to contact or involve law enforcement.<b=
r><br>3. All communications between DAS and OPRD concerning me, including a=
ny consultation, guidance, or technical assistance provided by DAS to OPRD =
regarding my dismissal, my exclusion, my correspondence, my public records =
requests, the archive at oprdvolunteerabuse.org, or the March 24, 2026 poli=
ce visit.<br><br>4. All communications between DAS and Oregon State Police,=
 the Oregon Department of Justice, the Office of the Governor, or any feder=
al agency concerning me.<br><br>5. All records reflecting the disclosure of=
 my personal information, including my date of birth, my residence, or my v=
olunteer file, to any person or agency outside OPRD.<br><br>6. The followin=
g policy and training records, without regard to date:<br><br>(a) Statewide=
 Policy 50.010.02, Violence-Free Workplace, in both the version effective 1=
1/1/2024 and the superseded version effective 02/01/2019.<br><br>(b) Statew=
ide Policy 50.010.04, Workplace Effects of Domestic Violence, Sexual Assaul=
t, and Stalking, and the accompanying online Toolkit referenced in 50.010.0=
2(4).<br><br>(c) The DAS-CHRO Violence and Weapons Free Workplace training =
required by 50.010.02(10), including all slides, scripts, scenarios, handou=
ts, and completion records.<br><br>(d) Any agency safety plan, procedure, g=
uidance, form, checklist, or assessment instrument used to carry out 50.010=
.02(4) or 50.010.02(6), including any used to assess reported incidents, an=
d any addressing application of the policy to volunteers or other non-emplo=
yees within the definition of &quot;others working in an agency.&quot;<br><=
br>(e) Any guidance, training, or written material issued by DAS or CHRO to=
 executive branch agencies concerning behavioral threat assessment, threat =
management teams, or workplace violence prevention teams.<br><br>(f) Any re=
cord identifying the agency directors, human resource sections, or safety s=
ections designated to administer 50.010.02 at the Oregon Parks and Recreati=
on Department, and any delegation of that authority. <br><br>7. All records=
 reflecting the number of behavioral threat assessments, workplace violence=
 assessments, or threat management processes initiated by executive branch =
agencies since January 1, 2023, in whatever aggregate or summary form DAS m=
aintains.<br><br>If any responsive record is withheld, please identify it b=
y date, author, recipient, and subject, and cite the specific exemption cla=
imed. If DAS is not the custodian of a particular record, please identify t=
he custodian rather than closing the request. ORS 192.311(2)(b) defines the=
 custodian to include a public body that owns or retains a record, and DAS =
is the custodian of its own correspondence.<br><br>I request a fee waiver. =
Disclosure of these records is in the public interest. The question of whet=
her an authority created to prevent violence has been used against a volunt=
eer for documenting his own treatment is a matter of public concern, and th=
e resulting records bear on the conduct of two state agencies toward a memb=
er of the public.<br><br>Notice regarding two prior requests: I intend to p=
etition the Attorney General under ORS 192.411 concerning requests R000879 =
and R000885, which DAS has not resolved in a manner consistent with its obl=
igations under ORS 192.311 to 192.478. That petition will be filed this wee=
k and published with its exhibits.<br><br>I have an active public records p=
etition before the Attorney General concerning Oregon State Police, PR27478=
, and I have given notice of intent to file a claim under ORS 30.275 concer=
ning the March 24, 2026 police visit. Please treat all records identified a=
bove as subject to litigation hold.<br><br>Robert Samuel White<br>rsw@rswfi=
